{"description":"Planned 2026-09-27. On SIGTERM or SIGINT, the --http server (a single design or a registry root):
1. stops accepting connections;
2. waits for in-flight requests up to a grace period (configurable, shorter than a container's stop timeout);
3. closes every open design's store and ends its sessions;
4. then exits.
Without this, a deploy that stops the process can end a write mid-way, and every open store is closed by the process dying rather than by its owner.","name":"An HTTP server told to stop drains its in-flight requests within a grace period and closes every open store before exiting","provenance":"authored","status":"realized","tier":"operational"}
